<%#
  T-37 / FR-72 — THE DROP REFERENCE, IN THE SIDEBAR, GENERATED AT RUNTIME.

  §9b.1 clause 2: *"the reference sidebar is **rendered from it at runtime**: every drop,
  every accessor, its type, whether it is a batch accessor, and a copyable `{{ … }}`
  snippet. Consequence worth stating plainly: documentation drift for the drop layer becomes
  structurally impossible, and the alternative — a hand-written wiki page — is exactly the
  artefact that is stale in every Redmine plugin."*

  "At runtime" is literal: `DropReference.sections` asks each drop class what a template can
  reach (`Liquid::Drop.invokable_methods`) on this request. A drop that loses an accessor
  loses it here in the same deploy, with nobody editing a view — and the same generator
  writes `docs/drop-reference.md`, which `script/gates/drop_reference_parity.sh` holds equal
  to a fresh generation in both directions.

  --- `<details>` AND NOT A SEARCH BOX ---

  Fifteen drops and 127 accessors do not fit in a Redmine sidebar open, and a filter would
  need JavaScript — which the editor deliberately does not depend on ([OQ-M], and the
  `<textarea>` above). `<details>`/`<summary>` is HTML, works closed on every browser this
  plugin supports, and the first section is open because it is the one an author wants.

  --- WHY THE SNIPPET IS THE LINK TEXT AND THERE IS NO COPY BUTTON ---

  A copy button is a JavaScript dependency for something a browser already does with a
  double-click. The snippet is `<code>` so it selects as one word.
%>
<h3><%= l(:label_reporter_drop_reference) %></h3>

<p><em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_drop_reference_info) %></em></p>

<% RedmineReporterDashboards::Liquid::DropReference.sections.each_with_index do |section, index| %>
  <details class="reporter-drop-reference" <%= 'open' if index.zero? %>>
    <summary><%= section.variable %></summary>
    <%# `reached_from` and `note` are English by construction — they name Liquid constructs
        (`{% for %}`, `issue.custom_field_values[42]`) and drop class names, which are not
        translated anywhere in this plugin. The LABELS around them are keys. Same split as
        the linter's rule messages one panel up. %>
    <p class="reporter-drop-reference-note"><%= section.reached_from %></p>
    <% if section.note %>
      <p class="reporter-drop-reference-note"><%= section.note %></p>
    <% end %>
    <ul class="reporter-drop-reference-list">
      <% section.accessors.each do |accessor| %>
        <li>
          <code><%= accessor.snippet(section.variable) %></code>
          <span class="reporter-drop-reference-type">
            <%= accessor.of ? "#{accessor.type} (#{accessor.of})" : accessor.type %>
            <%# THE ONE PIECE OF METADATA AN AUTHOR CANNOT GUESS: reading this in a
                `{% for %}` costs no extra query, because §3.4's batch registry loaded it
                for the whole page. Its absence is not marked — a badge on 121 of 127 rows
                is noise, and the useful signal is the exception. %>
            <% if accessor.batch? %>
              <span class="reporter-drop-reference-batch"
                    title="<%= l(:text_reporter_drop_reference_batch) %>"><%=
                l(:label_reporter_drop_reference_batch) %></span>
            <% end %>
          </span>
          <% if accessor.note %>
            <span class="reporter-drop-reference-note"><%= accessor.note %></span>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </details>
<% end %>
